body: |-
  ## 6 open calls (1 blocking authoring)

  1. **PARA 451 numbering [BLOCKING]** — entry ids baked into every file:
     - (A) Recommended: ship at PARA 451 sibling-to-401, mark 401 agent entries as v6.1 retirement candidates
     - (B) Number 050 or 150 — agents become early-curriculum topic
     - (C) Replace 401 in-place — risky (restructures 401 path)

  2. Rune framing for Phase A — describe at v6.0.3 surface (advisory planner/reporter, no authority claims yet). v6.1 PARA 551 covers authority modes. Confirm.

  3. Scholar+Sheila self-attribution in `N-para-451-partners-primitive` — recommended yes, teach the partners pattern by being one.

  4. `N-para-451-tiers` scoping — strictly about MODEL tier (opus/sonnet/haiku); single forward-compat callout for v6.1 NOTEBOOK tier (avoid concept collision).

  5. Pack version bump cadence — single bump or split into foundation + partners/auto-rostering chunks?

  6. Identity model entry depth — teach archetype concept even though no first-class `archetype` field in AgentProfile yet (forward-compat callout) OR ship the field first?

  ## Course structure
  - Title: PARA 451: Agents Foundations
  - Tagline: Meet the team. Learn what each agent does and when to call them.
  - Difficulty: Beginner (one intermediate sub-track entry on partners deep-dive)
  - Time: 35min skim, 75-90min full mastery
  - Single ordered path LP-para-451; Phase B = separate PARA 551 course

  ## Surprise to flag up
  The premise "ZERO entries on agents" was inaccurate. The real problem is "agents are taught wrong, in the wrong place" — stale content locked in an advanced course beginners never reach. Phase A fixes both by replacing the locked-stale path with a beginner-accessible foundation; v6.1 archives the 401 stales.
